1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,900
 Okay, so let's practice how to do good prompting.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:06,340
 So let's go in their chats and we're going to select a model.

3
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:11,620
 We're going to select an anthropic and then we select a Cloud 3 Hiku.

4
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:17,280
 We'll just write a prompt, write me a travel itinerary.

5
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:21,140
 This prompt is very naive, it's not very detailed.

6
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:26,560
 Here the model just responds, here is a seven-day trip and it shows

7
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:28,700
 Rome, Florence, and Venice, and Italy.

8
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:32,520
 So why not this is an answer that is possible for us to deal with,

9
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:35,520
 but it's not the one I want because I was not very precise.

10
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:39,160
 Instead, we want to use a framework we had of giving instructions,

11
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:44,040
 giving context, giving input data, and then giving an output format.

12
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:47,800
 So under our code, under prompting, I've created prompted.txt.

13
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:50,120
 And we're going to use the first format.

14
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:53,060
 So the instructions, the context, and the output.

15
00:00:53,060 --> 00:00:55,400
 So let's have a look at what it is.

16
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:59,880
 So we're saying, hey, please create a three-day itinerary for Paris France.

17
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:04,360
 It should include visits to historical landmarks, art museums, and popular local restaurants.

18
00:01:04,360 --> 00:01:07,880
 You want good balance, you want to have suggestions for breakfast, lunch, and dinner.

19
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:08,840
 Here's the context.

20
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:13,480
 So we've never traveled to Paris before and we want to experience both the well-known and hidden gems.

21
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:16,680
 So of course, some people who have already been to Paris may want something different.

22
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:19,000
 So the context is very important.

23
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:22,200
 And then input data right now is just a three-day trip to Paris,

24
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:26,040
 but we may want to add articles that we've read in the news,

25
00:01:26,040 --> 00:01:30,040
 and this would be a good way to enhance the outcome of this prompt.

26
00:01:30,040 --> 00:01:32,600
 And then our put indicator is, what do we want?

27
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:37,880
 We want the travel itinerary with specific times, location, descriptions, and dining recommendations.

28
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:39,880
 So this is quite a complete prompt.

29
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:48,760
 And as you can see, now the model is telling us a lot of things about what to do on each specific day.

30
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:53,320
 And this is quite nice because, well, we are getting the recommendations we want for the exact

31
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:55,240
 prompt we cared about.

32
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:59,400
 So it really shows you the difference of quality of a good and a bad prompt.

33
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:05,000
 Now, we also must include, if we want to, improve it, negative prompting.

34
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,960
 And negative prompting is, what do we not want to see?

35
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:13,000
 So here, for example, do not include activities that are primarily for children or families

36
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:17,480
 and avoid overly touristy restaurants, and include anything that requires too much travel,

37
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:19,000
 except Versailles.

38
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,640
 So let's paste it and run it.

39
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:26,600
 And again, you can have a look at if this output was better than the previous one,

40
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,840
 or not based on the negative prompting.

41
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:31,880
 And we can do any kind of creative negative prompting.

42
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:34,680
 For example, we can say, hey, here is the instructions.

43
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:41,320
 And then do not recommend more than three activities per day.

44
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:43,160
 And we run it.

45
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:47,320
 And again, with the negative prompting, now we're getting less activities per day.

46
00:02:47,320 --> 00:02:51,480
 So it's a bit shorter day and maybe we'll have more time to do stuff in Paris.

47
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:54,120
 I cannot tell you if this is a good recommendation or not.

48
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:57,560
 I'll leave it in Paris, but AI can be sometimes surprising.

49
00:02:57,560 --> 00:03:00,440
 Anyway, if you would trust AI to organize your next travel,

50
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:04,200
 you know how to do it now and you know how to properly build a prompt for it.

51
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:05,560
 So I hope you liked it.

52
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:07,560
 And I will see you in the next lecture.

